syntax:
class Base {
protected:
    virtual void foo();
    int base_member;
};

class Derived : public Base {
protected:
    virtual void foo() override;
    int derived_member;
};

// Implementation notes:
// - Each class with virtual functions has a vtable.
// - Objects contain a hidden vptr pointing to the class's vtable.
// - Inheritance causes the derived object layout to include base subobjects.
// - Constructor initializes vptrs; destructors clean up vtables if needed.
// - Compiler may optimize vtable placement and access.
// - Multiple inheritance introduces multiple vptrs and complex layout.
// - Virtual function calls are indirect through vtable lookups.
// - Compiler optimizations include vtable merging, devirtualization, and inlining.
